{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/262585-demons-and-blood-bonds","id":262585,"title":"Demons and Blood Bonds.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-21T19:20:20-07:00","id":262585,"title":"Demons and Blood Bonds.","content":"So a question came up while figuring out details for a game: can Demons be Blood Bound? If they can, does it always count, or if a vampire Blood Bonds a Cover, is only that Cover Blood Bound? Etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Of course, in general, I am of the opinion that any Demon stupid enough to be Blood Bound should just get tossed back into the God-Machine, but the question still needs answering for this particular scenario.<br /> <br /> Additional question: can a Demon be fed from? I assume they can while in Cover, but what about in their Demonic Form? If their blood is something else --Aether, petrol, toxic fumes, maybe they don't have blood at all--<br /> <br /> Opinions? <i>he asked, batting his lashes at Matt or Rose in particular</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T19:51:36-07:00","id":262607,"title":"","content":"Anyone can be blood bonded in 2nd edition. So I wouldn't say Demons are an exception there. Feeding on their Covers would probably work as if you're feeding on a human. Feeding on their Demonic Form is insane, but I imagine it'd need that A Taste of the Strange merit or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T19:53:55-07:00","id":262609,"title":"","content":"Can you point me at where it says anyone can be Blood Bond in 2e? I don't recall there being any 'other supernaturals can now be blood bound'. Since the opposite was true for the previous edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T20:03:32-07:00","id":262612,"title":"","content":"I would say that , either way, NOT acting Bloodbound counts as a Compromise if they are acting as a human, since a human should be bound, and one that isn't is obviously strange. My 2 cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T20:47:40-07:00","id":262629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/262585-demons-and-blood-bonds?p=262612#post262612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that , either way, NOT acting Bloodbound counts as a Compromise if they are acting as a human, since a human should be bound, and one that isn't is obviously strange. My 2 cents.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Blood Bonds aren't automatic. You can resist them. So if the Blood Bond wouldn't take by default, the vampire might just think the mortal resisted. Sure, it's weird, but it's not impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T21:27:08-07:00","id":262646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/262585-demons-and-blood-bonds?p=262609#post262609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you point me at where it says anyone can be Blood Bond in 2e? I don't recall there being any 'other supernaturals can now be blood bound'. Since the opposite was true for the previous edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.zaahc96hxwec\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.zaahc96hxwec\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.zaahc96hxwec\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.zaahc96hxwec </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here you go.<br /> <br /> FYI: <i>Kindred </i>may spend a Willpower to resist the Vinculum. Mortals have no such recourse. Whether other supernaturals can also resist like Vampires can is subject to individual storytellers. I would probably err on the side of kindness and allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T22:59:12-07:00","id":262680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/262585-demons-and-blood-bonds?p=262646#post262646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.zaahc96hxwec\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.zaahc96hxwec\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.zaahc96hxwec\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.zaahc96hxwec </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here you .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's totally accurate. Demons can be blood bounded and this is not a case to have a compromise roll by defaut, perhaps if you feel the cover would normally be very independent and now others might think there is something wrong with this all new sudden obsession/passion/slavery. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't allow a vampire to feed on the demonic forms. I believe biting metal can only break your jaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T03:59:34-07:00","id":262756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/262585-demons-and-blood-bonds?p=262607#post262607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feeding on their Demonic Form is insane, but I imagine it'd need that A Taste of the Strange merit or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think vampires have ever needed a Merit to feed on other monsters in Requiem. Taste of the Strange, and its 2e equivalent Unnatural Affinity, aren't necessary to draw sustenance from a monster as if it were a human being; their effect is to let you count it as drinking Kindred vitae for the purposes of elder feeding restrictions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amadeu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/262585-demons-and-blood-bonds?p=262680#post262680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't allow a vampire to feed on the demonic forms. I believe biting metal can only break your jaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more relevant, but I'd probably take it case-by-case, as demonic forms can vary a great deal, and not all of them are made of stone and metal. If you're a glowing Adonis with wings of glass, I'd probably allow it and maybe improvise some weird side effects of drinking Unchained blood. If you're a ball of light or a swarm of quicksilver globules, though, yeah, hard to find a vein there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 09-22-2014, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T20:12:25-07:00","id":264359,"title":"","content":"Thanks, guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T03:13:41-07:00","id":266071,"title":"","content":"As a huge vampire player (and semi Demon one), I'd like to throw in some input as well.<br /> Anyways, typical situation is either Demon drinks the blood in his demonic form or in his Covers. <br /> Now if it's demonic form, he may get a chance to resist it (or not) depending on a Storyteller. At least I'd allow the chance to resist.<br /> If he's in his Covers, the Cover get's automatically Bound and the Demon get's the chance to resist it under the normal rules. Since Covers can have individual conditions, then the Cover has the Bound condition, and should the Demon ignore it, it might be a compromise. (Of Course, I'd say it's a compromise only after a second or third drink. Drink #1 ain't strong enough, imo)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}